In NetHack, the word "maze" specifically refers to a *randomly generated*
part of the dungeon. The Valley has no random parts; the beginning is more
like a cavern (as in the Mines), while the last bit (above Moloch's
temple) is also hardly a maze: it's has only one crossing.

Note that "maze" is also used in the sources, it specifically refers to a
randomly generated dungeon part. The Castle has two mazes, Gehennom has
lots of mazes, often combined with a non-random level part, and one of the
Mines' bottoms also has a maze.

